ter rounded-lg font-semibold transition-all bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-emerald-100 border border-emerald-200\",\"children\":\"Persian\"}],[\"$\",\"$Le\",\"turkish\",{\"href\":\"/names/hindu/origin/turkish/1\",\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg font-semibold transition-all bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-emerald-100 border border-emerald-200\",\"children\":\"Turkish\"}],[\"$\",\"$Le\",\"indian\",{\"href\":\"/names/hindu/origin/indian/1\",\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg font-semibold transition-all bg-emerald-600 text-white\",\"children\":\"Indian\"}],[\"$\",\"$Le\",\"english\",{\"href\":\"/names/hindu/origin/english/1\",\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg font-semibold transition-all bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-emerald-100 border border-emerald-200\",\"children\":\"English\"}],[\"$\",\"$Le\",\"other\",{\"href\":\"/names/hindu/origin/other/1\",\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg font-semibold transition-all bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-emerald-100 border border-emerald-200\",\"children\":\"Other\"}]]}]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center py-16\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":\"No Names Found\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600\",\"children\":[\"No names found from \",\"indian\",\" origin. Try another origin.\"]}]]}]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The History & Culture of \",\"Indian\",\" Origin \",\"Hindu\",\" Baby Names\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The \",\"Indian\",\" origin represents one of the richest linguistic and cultural traditions in naming history. Names from this region have shaped identities across \",0,\"+ entries in our database, spanning centuries of cultural exchange, migration, and adaptation. The historical depth of \",\"Indian\",\" naming traditions connects modern families to ancient civilizations that flourished along trade routes, in fertile river valleys, and within vibrant urban centers that served as centers of learning and culture.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Indian\",\" names within the \",\"Hindu\",\" tradition blend beautifully with religious naming customs, creating a unique synthesis of spiritual significance and linguistic beauty. These names maintain their authentic linguistic meaning while fitting seamlessly into \",\"Hindu\",\" cultural and spiritual contexts. The combination creates names that feel both historically rooted and contemporary — suitable for global families who want their children to carry a piece of this rich heritage forward into the modern world.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Throughout history, \",\"Indian\",\" naming conventions were deeply influenced by regional dialects, ruling dynasties, religious scholarship, and poetic movements. Many \",\"Indian\",\" names were originally given based on specific circumstances of birth, family aspirations, or spiritual significance. The poetic nature of \",\"Indian\",\" languages means that even practical names carry layers of metaphorical meaning — from nature imagery and celestial references to virtues like generosity, patience, and wisdom.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Popular \",\"Indian\",\" names in \",\"Hindu\",\" tradition often reflect core values: strength, beauty, devotion, knowledge, and grace. Names like those in our collection of \",0,\"+ \",\"Hindu\",\" \",\"Indian\",\" origin names have been carefully researched for accuracy in meaning and cultural context. Each one represents a story — of families who chose it, communities who cherished it, and children who have proudly borne it across generations.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600\",\"children\":[\"Preserving these naming traditions in a global context is more important than ever. As families dispersed across continents, \",\"Indian\",\" names traveled with them, adapting to new languages while retaining their essential character. Today, \",\"Hindu\",\" parents choosing \",\"Indian\",\" origin names are participating in a rich living tradition — connecting their children to a heritage that spans continents and centuries while celebrating the universal values that all cultures share.\"]}]]}]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Popular \",\"Indian\",\" Names & Naming Traditions for \",\"Hindu\",\" Families\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"When selecting a \",\"Indian\",\" origin name, consider these important factors: understand the authentic meaning in its original language, practice pronouncing it easily, consider family and cultural connections, evaluate potential nicknames, and think about how it sounds across a lifetime. Many \",\"Indian\",\" names have beautiful phonetic qualities — the melodic sounds of \",\"Sanskrit syllables and Hindi phonetics\",\" make them particularly appealing for families who appreciate linguistic beauty.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Many parents appreciate \",\"Indian\",\" origin names for their melodic quality and rich historical associations. These names often have beautiful phonetic structures that work well across different languages and cultures, making them excellent choices for multicultural families. The flexibility of \",\"Indian\",\" names means they can be easily combined with middle names from other traditions, allowing for creative and deeply personal naming choices that honor multiple heritages.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Use our tools to save favorites, compare meanings, and explore sibling name options. Each \",\"Indian\",\" name includes lucky number associations and origin details to enrich your naming journey. Consider how the meaning of a potential name might resonate with your hopes for your child — whether you hope they grow into qualities like wisdom, kindness, leadership, or creativity. Many \",\"Hindu\",\" families choose \",\"Indian\",\" names specifically for the virtues they embody.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600\",\"children\":[\"The process of choosing a \",\"Indian\",\" origin \",\"Hindu\",\" name is deeply personal but can also be a shared family experience. Grandparents, siblings, and extended family members often contribute suggestions and stories about names that have special significance across generations. We encourage you to use our database as a starting point for these important conversations, and to trust your instincts as you narrow down the perfect name for your little one.\"]}]]}]}]\n9:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-20\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-emerald-100 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer px-6 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors list-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\